---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { resolveRefs } from '@/content/references';

const total = (await getCollection('lessons')).length;
const coreRefs = resolveRefs([
  'vonNeumannMorgenstern1944',
  'nash1950',
  'schelling1960',
  'axelrod1984',
  'osborneRubinstein1994',
  'gibbons1992',
]);
---
<BaseLayout active="about" totalLessons={total} title="About">
  <div class="about">
    <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
    <h1>Play first, then formalise</h1>
    <p>Game theory has a habit of being counterintuitive. Betrayal can be the rational move. Being predictable gets you beaten. A small preference can segregate a whole city. You believe these once you have felt them, so every lesson lets you act before it explains, then hands you the definition and the argument.</p>

    <div class="princ"><span class="n">1</span><div>You commit a guess or a move first. The gap between your guess and what happens is where the learning is.</div></div>
    <div class="princ"><span class="n">2</span><div>The concrete game comes before the notation. Symbols arrive once the idea is already in your hands.</div></div>
    <div class="princ"><span class="n">3</span><div>Earlier ideas keep coming back in later quizzes, so they stick instead of fading.</div></div>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2>References</h2>
      <ol class="refs">{coreRefs.map((html) => <li set:html={html} />)}</ol>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2>Your data</h2>
      <p>Your progress is stored only in this browser. Nothing is sent anywhere. You can take it with you or wipe it any time.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn ghost" id="exportBtn">Export progress</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="resetBtn">Reset progress</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="note">This is an early build. The first lessons are live; the full course runs to 63 lessons plus a set of real-world cases, from the Prisoner's Dilemma to mechanism design.</div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { reset, exportJSON } from '@/lib/progress';

  function toast(msg: string) {
    const t = document.getElementById('toast');
    if (!t) return;
    t.textContent = msg;
    t.classList.add('show');
    setTimeout(() => t.classList.remove('show'), 2400);
  }

  document.getElementById('resetBtn')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (confirm('Reset all progress on this device? This cannot be undone.')) {
      reset();
      toast('Progress reset');
    }
  });

  document.getElementById('exportBtn')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    try {
      const blob = new Blob([exportJSON()], { type: 'application/json' });
      const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
      const a = document.createElement('a');
      a.href = url;
      a.download = 'game-theory-progress.json';
      document.body.appendChild(a);
      a.click();
      a.remove();
      URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
    } catch {
      toast('Export not available here');
    }
  });
</script>
